96","url":null,"note":"Field-calibrated Al₂SiO₅ triple point, the basis of polymorph thermobarometry.","tags":["thermobarometry"]},{"citation":"Whitney, D.L. (2002). Coexisting andalusite, kyanite, and sillimanite: sequential formation of three Al<sub>2</sub>SiO<sub>5</sub> polymorphs during progressive metamorphism near the triple point, Sivrihisar, Turkey. <i>American Mineralogist</i> 87, 405–416.","doi":"10.2138/am-2002-0404","url":null,"note":"Textures and crystallization sequence of all three polymorphs.","tags":["petrology"]},{"citation":"Kerrick, D.M. (ed.) (1990). <i>The Al<sub>2</sub>SiO<sub>5</sub> Polymorphs</i>. Reviews in Mineralogy 22.","doi":"10.1515/9781501509094","url":null,"note":"The standard review of Al₂SiO₅ crystallography, occurrence and phase equilibria.","tags":["review"]}],"cells":[{"id":"L1m","row":0,"col":0,"label":"L1m","sub":"","title":"L1m: aspect 3:1 along c · square {110} prism","description":"aspect 3:1 along c; square {110} prism.","default":false,"params":{"face_distances":{"110":1.0,"100":null,"010":null,"230":null,"001":0.5},"cap_translation":3.796467,"scale":0.30753034,"planes":{"110":0.30753034,"001":1.32129387}},"fractions":{"110":0.8958,"001":0.1042},"metrics":{"volume":1.0,"surface_area":7.26026,"rsv":0.41321,"sphericity":0.66609,"aspect":3.0},"geometry":{"vertices":[[-0.4296,-0.0,-1.32129],[-0.0,0.44043,-1.32129],[0.0,-0.44043,-1.32129],[0.4296,0.0,-1.32129],[-0.0,0.44043,1.32129],[-0.4296,-0.0,1.32129],[0.4296,0.0,1.32129],[0.0,-0.44043,1.32129]],"faces":[{"form":"110","hkl":[1,1,0],"loop":[3,1,4,6]},{"form":"110","hkl":[-1,-1,0],"loop":[5,0,2,7]},{"form":"110","hkl":[-1,1,0],"loop":[1,0,5,4]},{"form":"110","hkl":[1,-1,0],"loop":[7,2,3,6]},{"form":"001","hkl":[0,0,1],"loop":[6,4,5,7]},{"form":"001","hkl":[0,0,-1],"loop":[3,2,0,1]}]},"files":{"stl":"models/stl/sillimanite/sillimanite_L1m.stl","step":"models/step/sillimanite/sillimanite_L1m.step"}},{"id":"L1o","row":0,"col":1,"label":"L1o","sub":"","title":"L1o: aspect 3:1 